hacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-129269" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b7121365a5651064a63e6ad7ea3d7b613dcf9341122c72f075f95529beee1ea"} {"question" "q-129269" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-129269" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-3,\\,1,\\,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨-4,\\,2,\\,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨-9,\\,2,\\,5⟩"] ["math" "⟨4,\\,-2,\\,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨4,\\,1,\\,1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-129269" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨4,\\,-2,\\,2⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-98216" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate \n${\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{3}^{6}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨8,\\,-6,\\,15⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{4}^{6}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-98216" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{6}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{6}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{3}^{6}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{4}^{6}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{3}^{6}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{4}^{6}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨8,\\,-6,\\,15⟩-⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨10,\\,-9,\\,11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-98216" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b7121365a5651064a63e6ad7ea3d7b613dcf9341122c72f075f95529beee1ea"} {"question" "q-98216" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-98216" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨10,\\,-9,\\,11⟩"] ["math" "⟨10,\\,14,\\,-7⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,\\,-12,\\,11⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,\\,-9,\\,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨8,\\,-4,\\,3⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-98216" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨10,\\,-9,\\,11⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-96943" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate \n${\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨8,\\,-6,\\,15⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-96943" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩-⟨8,\\,-6,\\,15⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-10,\\,9,\\,-11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-96943" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b7121365a5651064a63e6ad7ea3d7b613dcf9341122c72f075f95529beee1ea"} {"question" "q-96943" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-96943" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-1,\\,-3,\\,11⟩"] ["math" "⟨-10,\\,9,\\,-11⟩"] ["math" "⟨10,\\,6,\\,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨7,\\,2,\\,11⟩"] ["math" "⟨9,\\,1,\\,-1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-96943" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-10,\\,9,\\,-11⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-98279" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${\\int }_{2}^{3}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=6\\,i-4\\,j+3\\,k$ \nand \n$c=i-2\\,j+2\\,k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-98279" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{3}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\times {\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{3}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(i-2\\,j+2\\,k)\\times (6\\,i-4\\,j+3\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 6 & -4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-6+8)i-(3-12)j+(-4+12)k \\\\  & =2\\,i+9\\,j+8\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-98279" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b7121365a5651064a63e6ad7ea3d7b613dcf9341122c72f075f95529beee1ea"} {"question" "q-98279" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-98279" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\,i-6\\,j+8\\,k"] ["math" "2\\,i+9\\,j+8\\,k"] ["math" "2\\,i-9\\,j-8\\,k"] ["math" "i+6\\,j+9\\,k"] ["math" "i-6\\,j-9\\,k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-98279" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\,i+9\\,j+8\\,k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-32300" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}\\,i+\\,j+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,k,$ \n$c=i+u\\,j-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,k,$\nand \n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=0,$ what is the value of $u?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-32300" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The dot product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the dot-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(i+u\\,j-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,k)\\cdot (\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}\\,i+\\,j+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}+u-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8} \\\\  & =u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=0,$ we must have $u=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-32300" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b7121365a5651064a63e6ad7ea3d7b613dcf9341122c72f075f95529beee1ea"} {"question" "q-32300" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-32300" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-32300" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-32511" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${\\int }_{1}^{2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=({e}^{-1}-{e}^{-2})\\,i+{e}^{2}\\,j+(2{e}^{-1}-3{e}^{-2})\\,k$ \nand \n$c={e}^{2}\\,i+{e}^{-2}\\,j-{e}^{2}\\,k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-32511" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The dot product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the dot-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =({e}^{2}\\,i+{e}^{-2}\\,j-{e}^{2}\\,k)\\cdot (({e}^{-1}-{e}^{-2})\\,i+{e}^{2}\\,j+(2{e}^{-1}-3{e}^{-2})\\,k) \\\\  & ={e}^{2}\\cdot ({e}^{-1}-{e}^{-2})+{e}^{-2}\\cdot {e}^{2}-{e}^{2}\\cdot (2{e}^{-1}-3{e}^{-2}) \\\\  & =e-1+1-2e+3 \\\\  & =3-e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-32511" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b7121365a5651064a63e6ad7ea3d7b613dcf9341122c72f075f95529beee1ea"} {"question" "q-32511" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-32511" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2+e"] ["math" "2-e"] ["math" "3+e"] ["math" "3-2e"] ["math" "3-e"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-32511" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3-e"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-32522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=4\\,i+2\\,k$ \nand \n$c=i+j-k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-32522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(i+j-k)\\times (4\\,i+2\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(2+4)j+(0-4)k \\\\  & =2i-6j-4k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-32522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b7121365a5651064a63e6ad7ea3d7b613dcf9341122c72f075f95529beee1ea"} {"question" "q-32522" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-32522" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2i-2j+4k"] ["math" "2i+2j-4k"] ["math" "2i-6j-4k"] ["math" "4i-6j+2k"] ["math" "i+6j+2k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-32522" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2i-6j-4k"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-129292" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${\\int }_{1}^{4}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={e}^{2}\\,i-\\,j+e\\,k$ \nand \n$c={e}^{-1}\\,i+j+k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-129292" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The dot product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{4}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the dot-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =({e}^{-1}\\,i+j+k)\\cdot ({e}^{2}\\,i-\\,j+e\\,k) \\\\  & =e-1+e \\\\  & =2e-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-129292" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b7121365a5651064a63e6ad7ea3d7b613dcf9341122c72f075f95529beee1ea"} {"question" "q-129292" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-129292" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1-e"] ["math" "2e-1"] ["math" "3e"] ["math" "e+1"] ["math" "e-2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "q-129292" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2e-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7c40295f4baed3c0cd6dc3d16d77866bf19804d9350263fccba5f104ae8390c"} {"question" "e-3019" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} [  3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) ] \\,\\textrm{d}t$ given that $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} \\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 16, \\: 2,\\: -2\\right\\rangle$ and $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2}\\mathbf g(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 2,-4,2\\right\\rangle .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/example-3019.json" "file_sha256" "b4325214312d2fe2a72d3d0a7c6ae0ef7fc9e2f2ffbf86b7e22b0d47f8fd7959"} {"question" "e-3019" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\big[ \\, 3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) \\, \\big] \\, \\textrm d t =  \\displaystyle {3\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t + \\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf g(t) \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[3f(t)+g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3⟨16,\\,2,\\,-2⟩+⟨2,\\,-4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨48,\\,6,\\,-6⟩+⟨2,\\,-4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨50,2,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/example-3019.json" "file_sha256" "b4325214312d2fe2a72d3d0a7c6ae0ef7fc9e2f2ffbf86b7e22b0d47f8fd7959"} {"question" "e-8688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate \n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^2\\mathbf f(t) + \\langle 1,\\:-1,\\:1\\rangle\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_2^0\\mathbf f(t) \\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle -3, \\: 2, \\: 1 \\right\\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/example-8688.json" "file_sha256" "5d5fa9256f5c11d4a41de07d95a1c885d0d8124bd806e95348707baa917c3ee8"} {"question" "e-8688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨-3,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)+⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩+⟨t,\\,-t,\\,t⟩{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩+⟨2,\\,-2,\\,2⟩\\text{ } \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,-4,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/example-8688.json" "file_sha256" "5d5fa9256f5c11d4a41de07d95a1c885d0d8124bd806e95348707baa917c3ee8"} {"question" "e-3020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate \n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle \\dfrac{3}{2}, \\: 1, \\: 3 \\right\\rangle$\nand\n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 0, \\: 2, \\: 6 \\right\\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/example-3020.json" "file_sha256" "203f27b71cbdb193ed73d4978a08ef8e94342401b0256735cf0a638d2578da86"} {"question" "e-3020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the adjacent intervals, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t+\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t = \n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t - \\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,6⟩-⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\,1,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{3}{2},\\,1,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/example-3020.json" "file_sha256" "203f27b71cbdb193ed73d4978a08ef8e94342401b0256735cf0a638d2578da86"} {"question" "e-3021" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\displaystyle {\\int_0^1 }  \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t)  \\, \\textrm d t$ \ngiven that \n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm d t = \\mathbf i-3\\,\\mathbf j-4\\,\\mathbf k$ \nand \n$\\mathbf c=\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/example-3021.json" "file_sha256" "c03273a86020ea3e0bd108a41c3391276aa81a13a9aeed0d709722553282641e"} {"question" "e-3021" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int_0^1 } \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t =  \\mathbf c \\times {\\int_0^1 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t  .\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(j-k)\\times (i-3\\,j-4\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-4-3)i-(0+1)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =-7\\,i-\\,j-\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057355/example-3021.json" "file_sha256" "c03273a86020ea3e0bd108a41c3391276aa81a13a9aeed0d709722553282641e"}] "usage" {"e-3019" [] "e-3021" [] "e-3020" [] "q-96943" [] "e-8688" []} "basis" 1849 "retractions" [[17592186120482 :question/problem "Calculate\n\n$∫_{1}^{2}f(t)dt$\ngiven that\n$∫_{1}^{3}f(t)dt = ⟨ - 2, 3, 4⟩$\nand\n$∫_{2}^{3}f(t)dt = ⟨8,-6, 15⟩$."] [17592186119477 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} [3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t)] \\,\\textrm{d}t$ given that $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} \\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 16, \\: 2,\\: -2\\right\\rangle$ and $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2}\\mathbf g(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 2,-4,2\\right\\rangle$."] [17592186119477 :question/worked-solution "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int_0^2} \\big[ \\, 3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) \\, \\big] \\, \\textrm d t = \\displaystyle {3\\int_0^2} \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t + \\displaystyle {\\int_0^2} \\mathbf g(t) \\, \\textrm d t\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{2}[3f(t) + g(t)]dt &= 3∫_{0}^{2}f(t)dt + ∫_{0}^{2}g(t)dt \\\\\n&= 3⟨16, 2,-2⟩ + ⟨2,-4, 2⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨48, 6,-6⟩ + ⟨2,-4, 2⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨50, 2,-4⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186119622 :question/problem "Calculate\n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^2\\mathbf f(t) + \\langle 1,\\:-1,\\:1\\rangle\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_2^0\\mathbf f(t) \\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle -3, \\: 2, \\: 1 \\right\\rangle$."] [17592186119622 :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{2}f(t)dt &= - ∫_{2}^{0}f(t)dt \\\\\n&= - ⟨ - 3, 2, 1⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨3,-2,-1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{2}f(t) + ⟨1,-1, 1⟩dt &= ∫_{0}^{2}f(t)dt + ∫_{0}^{2}⟨1,-1, 1⟩dt \\\\\n&= ⟨3,-2,-1⟩ + ⟨t,-t, t⟩ \\mid _{0}^{2} \\\\\n&= ⟨3,-2,-1⟩ + ⟨2,-2, 2⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨5,-4, 1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186119478 :question/problem "Calculate\n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle \\dfrac{3}{2}, \\: 1, \\: 3 \\right\\rangle$\nand\n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 0, \\: 2, \\: 6 \\right\\rangle$."] [17592186119478 :question/worked-solution "Using the adjacent intervals, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t+\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t = \\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t - \\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{-1}^{0}f(t)dt &= ∫_{-1}^{1}f(t)dt - ∫_{0}^{1}f(t)dt \\\\\n&= ⟨0, 2, 6⟩ - ⟨\\frac{3}{2}, 1, 3⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - \\frac{3}{2}, 1, 3⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186119479 :question/problem "Find $\\displaystyle {\\int_0^1} \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm d t = \\mathbf i-3\\,\\mathbf j-4\\,\\mathbf k$\nand\n$\\mathbf c=\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k$."] [17592186119479 :question/worked-solution "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int_0^1} \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t = \\mathbf c \\times {\\int_0^1} \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t\n$$\n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{1}c \\cdot f(t)dt &= c \\cdot ∫_{0}^{1}f(t)dt \\\\\n&= (j - k) \\cdot (i - 3j - 4k) \\\\\n&=\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{vmatrix}i -\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{vmatrix}j +\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\\n&= (-4 - 3)i - (0 + 1)j + (0 - 1)k \\\\\n&=-7i - j - k\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186119367 17592186119368 17592186119369 17592186119370 17592186119371] "immutable_fields" [[17592186119366 :answer-field/correct] [17592186119366 :answer-field/id] [17592186119366 :answer-field/key] [17592186119366 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
